## 🩸 Blood Sugar & Diabetes Markers

* Fasting Blood Glucose: 70 - 99 mg/dL — Liquid fuel baseline; keeping this stable permanently deletes mid-day brain fog.
* Postprandial Glucose: < 140 mg/dL — Blood sugar measured exactly 2 hours after consuming a meal.
* Hemoglobin A1C: < 5.7% — The critical 3-month average curve of your systemic glucose control.
* Fasting Insulin: 2.6 - 24.9 mcIU/mL — Real-time marker of pancreatic strain and early metabolic efficiency.
* C-Peptide: 0.5 - 2.0 ng/mL — Direct mirror of internal insulin production levels.

## 🧫 Complete Blood Count (CBC)

* Red Blood Cell Count (RBC) - Men: 4.32 - 5.72 million cells/mcL — Oxygen transport capacity for cellular energy.
* Red Blood Cell Count (RBC) - Women: 3.90 - 5.03 million cells/mcL — Tailored baseline oxygen carrier metric for females.
* White Blood Cell Count (WBC): 4,500 - 11,000 cells/mcL — Total active defense shield of your biological immune system.
* Hemoglobin - Men: 13.2 - 16.6 g/dL — Iron-rich protein matrix carrying oxygen molecules through the blood.
* Hemoglobin - Women: 11.6 - 15.0 g/dL — Female reference target for structural blood oxygenation.
* Hematocrit - Men: 38.3% - 48.6% — Total percentage volume of blood made up of red cells.
* Hematocrit - Women: 35.5% - 44.9% — Female blood thickness and concentration baseline.
* Platelet Count: 150,000 - 450,000/mcL — Primary cell fragments responsible for rapid coagulation and structural repair.
* Mean Corpuscular Volume (MCV): 80 - 100 fL — Average physical size of your red blood cells; tells you if cells are malformed.
* Neutrophils: 40% - 60% of WBCs — Rapid-response immune cells designed to counter acute bacterial invaders.
* Lymphocytes: 20% - 40% of WBCs — Master immune cells handling deep viral defense and adaptive memory.
* Monocytes: 2% - 8% of WBCs — Heavy-duty cellular scavenger units that clean up internal debris and chronic waste.
* Eosinophils: 1% - 4% of WBCs — Specialized immune actors deployed against parasites and acute allergen spikes.
* Basophils: 0.5% - 1% of WBCs — Ultra-precise chemical triggers that release histamine to manage systemic inflammation.

## 🫀 Lipid Panel (Cholesterol & Heart Health)

* Total Cholesterol: < 200 mg/dL — Cumulative measure of structural sterols moving through your bloodstream.
