* HDL (Good) Cholesterol: > 40 mg/dL (Men) / > 50 mg/dL (Women) — High-density recycling units that sweep excess fats back to the liver.
* Triglycerides: < 150 mg/dL — Unused caloric energy floating as fat cells; high levels heavily drive cognitive sluggishness.
* VLDL Cholesterol: 2 - 30 mg/dL — Very low-density lipoproteins carrying internal fats directly to your tissues.

