* Creatinine - Women: 0.59 - 1.04 mg/dL — Tailored muscle waste tracking metric for females.
* eGFR (Glomerular Filtration Rate): > 90 mL/min — Your kidneys' literal processing speed; rates below 90 indicate filtration drag.
* Total Protein: 6.0 - 8.3 g/dL — Combined concentration of albumin and globulins building your body's structural matrix.
* Albumin: 3.4 - 5.4 g/dL — Main protein carrier molecule keeping fluids from leaking out of blood vessels into tissues.

## 🍁 Liver Function Panel (Hepatic)

* Bilirubin (Total): 0.1 - 1.2 mg/dL — Combined measurement of yellow waste bile pigment from old red blood cells.
* Bilirubin (Direct): < 0.3 mg/dL — Waste bile pigment that has been safely processed and conjugated by your liver cells.
* Alanine Aminotransferase (ALT): 7 - 55 U/L — Ultra-specific liver enzyme; leaks heavily into blood when cells face metabolic stress.
* Aspartate Aminotransferase (AST): 8 - 48 U/L — Metabolic enzyme found in liver, heart, and skeletal muscle tissue.
* Alkaline Phosphatase (ALP): 40 - 129 U/L — Enzyme heavily tied to your bile ducts, physical liver health, and bone turnover.
* Gamma-Glutamyl Transferase (GGT): 9 - 48 U/L — Sensitive indicator of bile duct irritation or toxicity stress inside the liver.
* Lactate Dehydrogenase (LDH): 140 - 280 U/L — General tissue breakdown enzyme; spikes during broad systemic damage.

